course: dictionary
lesson: 4057
title: Genetics: how features are passed on
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Genetics is the science of how features, like eye colour, pass from parents to children. The parts that carry these features are called genes. «A monk called Gregor Mendel grew thousands of pea plants to learn how features pass from parents to their young, and his work started the science of genetics.» The clues are «science» and «pass from parents to their young»: genetics is about how features are handed on.
explain: The word has an adjective too. Genetic describes something that comes from genes, so a genetic feature is one passed on through genes. Someone's genetics are the genes they were born with, and those genes affect how they grow and look.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If you read «Her genetics made her tall», you can replace genetics with «the genes she was born with» and it still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: Genetics is the science of how features are passed from parents to children.
fact: Genes are the parts that carry features, such as eye colour, from parents to children.
fact: Genetics is a noun that takes a singular verb: «Genetics is fascinating.»
fact: Gregor Mendel studied pea plants in the 1860s and is called the father of genetics.
fact: DNA carries genes.
exercise: «A monk called Gregor Mendel grew thousands of pea plants to learn how features pass from parents to their young.» What is genetics about? | How to build castles | Only the colour of eyes | *How features are passed from parents to young | Plants growing in gardens
exercise: Leo says a child's genetics are the games they like to play. What does genetics really mean here? | The clothes they wear | Games they play at break time | Their favourite food | *The genes a person was born with
exercise: Which word is the adjective that means relating to genes? | *genetic | genuine | general | generous
test: Gregor Mendel is called the father of what? | Cooking | Football | Astronomy | *Genetics
test: Which part of a cell carries genes? | Bricks | *DNA | Rivers | Clouds
exam: A farmer uses genetics to breed stronger animals. Why does the farmer need genetics? | To paint the barn | To count the fields | To keep the animals warm in summer | *To understand how features are passed on to young animals
